    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently, the `MiniSessions.read` function calls `vim.cmd('silent! %bwipeout!')` and there is no way to modify this. There are some buffers that I would want to keep when switching sessions back and forth on the same neovim instance (ex. terminal buffers to preserve the process) but I am sure there are other conditions people may want to use to preserve some buffers when the read happens.\n\nI suggest an option in the config that defaults to:\n```lua\nfunction()\n  vim.cmd('silent! %bwipeout!')\nend\n```\n\nBut can be replaced by a user's own custom wipe function.\n\nThanks for all the hard work!",
