        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "To clarify, I mean keeping the exact same buffer pinned to the session that created it by using the `buflisted` flag (only show the buffer in the session it belongs to). For terminals specifically, this means it keeps its scroll back, running commands and etc instead of having the session create a new one terminal when you switch back to the session in the same neovim instance (without restarting neovim).\n\nAnyway, I don't think I'm explaining myself well enough and I don't want to waste anymore of your time so I will just keep using my custom implementation of `mini.session`.\n\nThanks for responding!",
